---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — CallLine" description="CallLine was built because small businesses deserve a professional phone system without enterprise complexity.">
  <div class="container max-w-3xl py-16 px-4 mx-auto">
    <article class="prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <h1>About CallLine</h1>

      <p class="lead text-muted-foreground text-lg">
        CallLine was built for a simple reason: small businesses deserve to sound professional without paying enterprise prices or wrestling with complex phone systems.
      </p>

      <h2>The Problem</h2>
      <p>
        Most small business owners piece together their phone setup over time — a personal cell number here, a Google Voice number there, maybe a voicemail app that doesn't sync with anything. Calls get missed. Voicemails sit unheard. Texts come in on three different phones. It works until it doesn't, and by then you've already lost the customer.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Approach</h2>
      <p>
        CallLine puts your calls, voicemails, and SMS into one dashboard. You get a real business number, set up call routing that matches how your team actually works, and never wonder if a voicemail got lost again. Every message gets transcribed. Every call gets logged. Every text stays connected to the customer conversation.
      </p>

      <h2>Who We're Built For</h2>
      <p>
        We built CallLine for the plumber who needs calls forwarded to whoever's on duty. The dentist's office that wants after-hours calls to go to voicemail with a professional greeting. The contractor who needs to text estimates from a business number instead of a personal cell. If you run a small business and your phone setup feels patched together, CallLine is for you.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>
        Make every business sound professional from the first ring. That's it. No buzzwords, no "revolutionizing communications." Just a phone system that works the way you need it to, at a price that makes sense.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
